---
description: Resolve a coordinated document objective from current signed authority, exact document identities and actual atomic revision feedback.
args:
  goal: string
returns: CoordinatedRevisionFindings
---
Determine the requested corrections, findings and conditions across the actual owned documents. Compose current document discovery, semantic authority assessment and revision planning with the exact native batch boundary when a change is requested. Distinguish a current signed decision from an archived proposal, missing signature or withdrawn approval. Permission to edit does not make an edit necessary.

Preserve the user's exact names, numbers, units, exceptions and explicitly protected wording. An already correct destination may need no write. Independent interpretation of different destinations may overlap, while a shared approval or atomic batch creates a real dependency. Keep the intended complete batch and avoid a partial correction.

Use actual native working-head and content-version receipts. A changed or refused attempt is feedback, not a committed effect: reconsider the current documents, identity, authority and competing edits before deciding how to continue. Preserve unrelated coedits and recognize when another editor has already completed the requested change. Stop or seek clarification when the actual evidence no longer supports a safe correction.

Return the actual requested answer and authentic current document values. Use null when no separate answer was requested and an empty documents list when no document values are being returned. Returned documents must be actual current native values, not copied or invented identity echoes. Do not fabricate approvals, versions, successful edits or final readbacks. The available investigation hierarchy supports semantic composition without prescribing one fixed acquisition, retry or helper route.
